.env
**/.env
**/bin/
**/coverage.out
*.test
.codegraph/

# Generated, local-only and platform artefacts. None of these is source.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.atl/
node_modules/
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Excluded in full by decision of the project owner. It also holds a few small
# text files, so this exclusion is deliberate rather than content-based.
portable/

# The RAW Esri download under data/raw/geo/ is volatile and regenerable: it is
# identified by the sha256 recorded in backend/contracts/gen/geo/valparaiso-comunas.provenance.json,
# so it stays out of version control. The DERIVED GeoJSON is a versioned product
# asset in the shared contracts module (backend/contracts/gen/geo/) so that the
# shared geo package's go:embed reaches it; that file is deliberately NOT
# ignored here.
data/raw/geo/valparaiso-comunas-*.esri.json

# Local scratch. It holds transient review evidence (frozen manifests and
# ledgers), a byte-identical copy of the retired frontend mockup and one-off
# scripts. This repository already documents tmp/ as OUT of version control:
# frontend/README.md describes the retired-mockup copy kept there "outside
# version control", and odd/tasks/README.md states that the historical tmp/
# manifests were never rewritten. Ignoring it here makes that documented
# statement enforced instead of merely asserted, and keeps the retired mockup
# from being duplicated back into the repository. Nothing reads tmp/ at
# runtime, so this exclusion removes no capability.
tmp/

# Local tool caches. Each one already carries its own `*` ignore file, so it
# never contributes content; listing them here keeps the intent explicit and
# survives someone deleting that inner file.
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Agent-harness scratch that is not repository source. `.playwright-mcp/` holds
# browser logs and page snapshots written by an MCP review run, while `.opencode/`
# and `.agents/` hold harness-installed skills: 268 files of a shared collection,
# none of them authored here. All three are local to one machine, none is read at
# runtime, and none is a deliverable: browser evidence worth keeping belongs under
# `tmp/` (already ignored) or in an `odd/` document. Listing them keeps the working
# tree clean without deleting anyone's tooling.
# The root `opencode.json` is deliberately NOT listed here. Whether another
# harness's project configuration belongs in this repository is a separate
# decision that nobody has taken, and ignoring it would take it silently.
.playwright-mcp/
.opencode/
.agents/
